#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0eb038c-5b51-5d7c-bdf5-f61c5f197752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447870} {:answer/id #uuid "971fa534-d27a-5df8-a351-be678116035b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "971fa534-d27a-5df8-a351-be678116035b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447871} :answer-field/id #uuid "40fcbc27-f09e-5d13-b63b-a3bfac864c91" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ba547b1-a183-561a-904b-acf399df45c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447872} {:answer/id #uuid "3477959e-ae28-590c-8534-0de29bece5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3477959e-ae28-590c-8534-0de29bece5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447873} :answer-field/id #uuid "d27d2a30-f6b5-5889-b3e8-3a1ab661f5a8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d226a48-bc9a-5c4f-b777-3375deb35e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447874} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd9c72e-2a23-5a4f-a198-740e3160f17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd9c72e-2a23-5a4f-a198-740e3160f17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447875} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab34820-b3b2-5e7d-b74b-405abb292421" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3976bf87-6856-55b9-92ed-31a90b18feea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447876} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f9c511-78a7-51fe-b700-8504529e7988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3976bf87-6856-55b9-92ed-31a90b18feea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447876} :answer-field/id #uuid "66584c33-4333-5200-8df1-e753f58cf7e7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3b977ec-88a0-5b97-96bf-4f197129ba2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107119" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$  and its subset $T$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 0 & c\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $T$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $T$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $T$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $T,$  then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ 0 & {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \nis also an element of $T.$ So, $T$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 0 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\alpha A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\alpha a & \\alpha b \\\\ 0 & \\alpha c\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nalso belongs to $T.$ So, $T$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $T$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b7a062-ef02-5c3f-be58-2979089ee22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448658} {:answer/id #uuid "02bb4b11-0438-5ec9-92c6-66b83c256443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02bb4b11-0438-5ec9-92c6-66b83c256443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448659} :answer-field/id #uuid "5766e842-2314-5895-8db7-4751b4c94230" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0996d368-54fe-5fd4-9bf0-df4943fd6bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448660} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b09607-682d-595c-a588-1556d569050a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8b09607-682d-595c-a588-1556d569050a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448661} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0891f16-1461-57df-b6e2-b382dea6c917" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40610275-2114-568a-a07d-62f96e0c7268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448662} {:answer/id #uuid "fce9af31-06d0-53cd-9d6d-6181d54abe52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fce9af31-06d0-53cd-9d6d-6181d54abe52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448663} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be66204-83a9-53b9-bf40-ec0cbfed1ab5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5517861-72ea-563c-8242-0d1107c91530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448664} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a78852-4e82-51a1-89eb-21889102a3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5517861-72ea-563c-8242-0d1107c91530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448664} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbda2e7-f5a7-5f72-bb3f-fdff336a3646" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d2def00-4689-55b3-90a3-9823d892535b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43773" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $K$ containing all constant functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $K$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $K$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $K$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is a constant function if $f(x)=\\text{const}$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The sum of two constant functions is a constant function. So, $K$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. The product of a constant function by a scalar is again a constant function. So, $K$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $K$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb97b679-ed73-5d50-b8f3-ebd938a5c69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454138} {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e1f700-4e27-590e-9aea-505c9d96d52c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b77c043e-6368-5cf0-87ba-b422015be2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454140} {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b0eb3f5-b781-5609-babf-762a182d38c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530ae441-da27-537e-a55c-72a1a7eaffa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454142} {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69bf366-d3cc-56cd-81b4-3fe0b32a22ef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} {:answer/id #uuid "74d6078b-e09a-5835-921b-48b69ffd8255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} :answer-field/id #uuid "57276cd0-38fc-5c29-abd0-eff90122f7d4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e8696fa-a30e-5b2e-a6f9-20152471933a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94621" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $H$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $H$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0+0=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a matrix such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0\\cdot k=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $H$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09540a12-93a1-56bb-83a7-26a8ee5238bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451985} {:answer/id #uuid "cb44a1ec-0c76-5e3a-9081-665a0f335bf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.ty